# This file is an A3IP installer bundle. Two pieces of installation
# knowledge live inside it:
#
#   * INSTALL.md -- the install procedure OUTLINE. Defines the numbered
#     Steps (typically 1 through ~11) and marks which Tier each step is.
#     Tier 2 steps state OUTCOMES the AI must reach; Tier 1 steps are
#     mechanical. Locate "=== FILE: INSTALL.md ===" in this bundle.
#
#   * adapters/runtime/<platform>/install-skill.md -- platform-specific
#     KNOWLEDGE for satisfying the Tier 2 outcomes on your runtime
#     (Cowork / Codex / Claude Code / Cursor / other). Describes
#     conventions, not commandments. Locate "=== FILE: adapters/runtime/
#     <your-platform>/install-skill.md ===".
#
# Before doing any install work, READ both artifacts. They are the
# authoritative source of install knowledge for this package on your
# platform. You are NOT expected to execute them as verbatim scripts --
# you are expected to reason about them and apply your judgment to the
# install in front of you.
#
# The failure mode to avoid: starting the install without consulting
# these artifacts. The "=== FILE: ===" markers describe what's in
# the bundle, not where each file goes at runtime. Improvising the
# install layout from raw file structure -- without first reading
# INSTALL.md's Steps and the adapter's conventions -- breaks the
# install contract.
#
# Note on tooling: the `a3ip` CLI builds bundles; it does NOT install
# them. Install is performed by the installing AI consulting INSTALL.md
# plus the runtime adapter, then applying that knowledge to the
# specific install in front of it.
